{"book":{"id":"book-red-star-tattoo-my-life-as-a-girl-revolutionary-sonja-larsen","slug":"red-star-tattoo-my-life-as-a-girl-revolutionary-sonja-larsen","title":"Red Star Tattoo: My Life as a Girl Revolutionary","authors":[{"id":"person-sonja-larsen","name":"Sonja Larsen"}],"isbn13":["9780345815279"],"subjects":["Biography"],"topics":["Evangelicalism & Christian Nationalism","Gender & Feminism","Religion & Religious Movements","Family, Childhood & Adoption"],"centralFigures":[],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Red%20Star%20Tattoo%3A%20My%20Life%20as%20a%20Girl%20Revolutionary%20Sonja%20Larsen","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=Red%20Star%20Tattoo%3A%20My%20Life%20as%20a%20Girl%20Revolutionary%20Sonja%20Larsen","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=Red%20Star%20Tattoo%3A%20My%20Life%20as%20a%20Girl%20Revolutionary%20Sonja%20Larsen","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=Red%20Star%20Tattoo%3A%20My%20Life%20as%20a%20Girl%20Revolutionary%20Sonja%20Larsen","publisher":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL25859505W"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-hilary-weston-nonfiction-wikipedia-hilary-weston-writers-trust-prize-for-nonfiction","source-open-library-red-star-tattoo-my-life-as-a-girl-revolutionary-sonja-larsen","source-open-library-summary-red-star-tattoo-my-life-as-a-girl-revolutionary-sonja-larsen"],"publicationYear":2016,"thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/15198791-L.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0.044,"accessibilityScore":0,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[{"id":"memoiristic","score":1,"confidence":"high","evidence":["catalog text contains \"memoir\"","catalog text contains \"my\"","catalog text contains \"personal history\"","memoir/autobiography subject or topic"]},{"id":"biographical","score":0.34,"confidence":"low","evidence":["biography subject or topic"]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"renownProfile":{"knowsBook":false,"publicFame":5,"criticalRenown":5,"controversy":5,"llmAffinity":78,"affinityResidual":9.48,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.12,"criticalRenown":0.1,"controversy":0.1,"llmAffinity":0.86},"tags":{"craft":"voice","evidence":"personal-experience","stance":"moral-seriousness"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"summary":"\"From hardscrabble Milwaukee to dreamy Hawaii, from turbulent Montreal to free-spirited California, Red Star Tattoo is Sonja Larsen's unforgettable memoir of a young life spent on the move. By the age of 16, Sonja joins a cult-like communist organization in Brooklyn in a spirit of idealism and hope--unaware of the dark nature of what awaits her. A small, skinny 8-year-old-girl holding a teddy bear stands by the side of a country road with a young man she barely knows. They're hitchhiking from a commune in Quebec to one in California. It is 1973 and somehow the girl's parents think this is a good idea. Sonja Larsen's is a childhood in which family members come and go and where radical politics take over her mother's life and her own. As a pregnant teen her mother had been thrown out of home in Milwaukee by her evangelical preacher father. Her aunt Suzie is gripped by schizophrenia, her behaviour so erratic she eventually loses custody of her daughter.^ And then there is her cousin Dana, shunted back and forth long-distance between her parents--Dana, whose own need to escape leads to unspeakable tragedy. Looking for a sense of family, searching to belong, to have your life mean something--this is what all these girls and young women have in common.","subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Women revolutionaries","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-red-star-tattoo-my-life-as-a-girl-revolutionary-sonja-larsen"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Women, united states, biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-red-star-tattoo-my-life-as-a-girl-revolutionary-sonja-larsen"},{"source":"open